# Generalized NHE $S\_s[N]\_O$: Polymorphic Direct-to-Silicon Logic Architecture Specification (v2.0)

## Abstract

This paper proposes the generalized NHE (Natural Hardware Embedding) $S\_s[N]\_O$ architecture, which directly maps software instructions to physical coordinates on a silicon substrate in a 1:1 manner, fundamentally eliminating the overhead of software abstraction layers and the limitations of the von Neumann architecture, which are chronic bottlenecks in modern computing.

By mathematically generalizing the existing specific slot (19-21-28) structure, we prove a mixed-radix orthogonal mapping formula (Generalized Orthogonal Mapping Formula) that is infinitely scalable and contractible (Scaling) from small sensor nodes to massive artificial general intelligence (AGI) accelerators without address collisions. Furthermore, we implement a polymorphic hardware-defined architecture (Polymorphic Soft-$S\_s\_O$) where the meanings of $S$ (Subject), $s$ (Signal), and $O$ (Output) are not fixed but can be arbitrarily mapped by the user according to the characteristics of the hardware substrate and application. We also present an arbiter-free (No-Arbiter) modular model compatible with both planar single-chips (Planar SoC) and heterogeneous multi-layer stacked ICs (Heterogeneous 3D Stacked IC).

